==German==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|goh|de}} {{term|gewinnan|lang=goh}}; cf. {{term|winnan|lang=goh}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|de}} {{recons|winnanan|lang=gem-pro}}, ultimately from {{etyl|ine-pro|de}} {{recons|wen-||to strive, wish, desire, love|lang=ine-pro}}. Compare Old English {{term|gewinnan|ġewinnan|lang=ang}}, Low German {{term|winnen|lang=nds}}, Dutch {{term|winnen|lang=nl}}, English {{term|win|lang=en}}, Norwegian {{term|vinne|lang=no}}, Swedish {{term|vinna|lang=sv}}.
 
